WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:05.580
In the last few years, Kevin Costner has transformed
himself from a big-screen legend into the

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:10.890
small-screen star of one of the most watched
shows on television Paramount Network's modern-day

00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:12.960
Western melodrama Yellowstone.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:18.980
Costner portrays John Dutton, the head of
a Montana ranching dynasty whose lusted-after

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:24.580
land borders the titular national park and
a reservation occupied by indigenous peoples.

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:26.580
"What's he saying?"

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.640
"He says that it's wrong for one man to own
all this.

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:32.740
And that you should share it with all the
people."

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:40.580
While Costner has always brought a certain
movie-star swagger to Yellowstone, the series

00:00:40.591 --> 00:00:45.370
has set itself apart from its competition
by taking advantage of its setting to infuse

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:47.360
a big-screen verve into its narrative.

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:52.280
As it happens, the show's Montana setting
was one of the biggest deciding factors for

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:56.260
Costner to make his first appearance on a
serialized TV series.

00:00:56.629 --> 00:01:02.059
Speaking at Deadline's The Contenders Emmys
presentation in April 2019, Costner revealed

00:01:02.059 --> 00:01:06.899
that the reason he agreed to star on Yellowstone
had everything to do with its location, which

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:10.540
he felt would remind audiences of the beauty
of the real world.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:11.260
He said:

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:16.520
"The idea of seeing wide open spaces, when
the land was almost like the Garden of Eden

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:21.210
[...] To know that places like this still
exist in our country, adding drama against

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:26.821
its backdrop, and actually understand in the
realest terms that the meat that arrives on

00:01:26.821 --> 00:01:29.890
our table is still coming from somewhere [...] We
don't see that enough.

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:32.940
I don't think that we get outside enough,
if you will."

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:38.340
Yellowstone is hardly Costner's first brush
with the wide open spaces of the American

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:41.299
West, or even the Western genre for that matter.

00:01:41.299 --> 00:01:45.689
The actor has frequently saddled up and hit
the dusty trails over the course of his career,

00:01:45.689 --> 00:01:52.740
breaking through in the 1985 actioner Silverado
before appearing in 1994's Wyatt Earp and

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:58.259
later producing, directing, and starring in
2003's Open Range a cinematic trifecta that

00:01:58.259 --> 00:02:03.850
Costner had previously tackled to the tune
of two Academy Awards when his wispy, anti-Western

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:07.420
drama Dances With Wolves graced screens back
in 1990.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:09.740
"I've always wanted to see the frontier."

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:13.100
"You want to see the frontier."

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:14.400
"Yes, sir.

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:16.500
Before it's gone."

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:22.900
In 2017, Costner revealed that he had co-written
a 10-hour-long Western project that he'd love

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:25.420
to direct for the big or small screen.

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:27.250
Speaking with Vulture, he shared:

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:31.180
"I have another Western I've co-written with
some people, and I would like to play out

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:33.820
the second half of my career directing more.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:38.070
I've constantly given the movies I've found
to directors who I thought could do it better,

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:42.060
but there are a lot of voices in my ear from
my family saying, 'You need to direct the

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:43.660
movies you fall in love with.'

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:44.820
So I think I will."

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:50.000
As for Yellowstone, the show continues to
make stark use of its stunning vistas, which

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:53.960
serve as a fascinating backdrop and counterpoint
to its modern-day setting.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:58.540
Though Costner hasn't yet helmed an episode
of the series, you can go ahead and add it

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:03.430
to the list of his memorable Western ventures
with the actor bringing as much drama, presence,

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:06.760
and majesty to the show as the Montana sky
itself.

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:11.940
You can also rest assured that Paramount Network
brass and series creator Taylor Sheridan will

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:16.420
be making full use of both on Yellowstone's
already greenlit third season.

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:21.580
Yellowstone's second season took a swing-for-the-fences
mentality in terms of its many narrative arcs,

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:27.070
and its finale delivered definitive ends to
a couple of the series' more compelling storylines

00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:31.840
with a mix of shootouts, kidnappings, and
plenty of mano-a-mano-type fisticuffs.

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:36.820
Though producers have already gone on record
that season 3 of Yellowstone will likely level

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:42.340
off a bit in terms of sub-manic melodrama
and unabashed bloodletting, it's a safe bet

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:47.600
that the show will still be steeped in searing
political and personal dramas for season 3.

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:53.520
What also won't change on Yellowstone season
3 is its stunning, sprawling Montana landscape

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:56.590
that Costner and series fans love so much.

00:03:56.590 --> 00:04:01.140
After all, the Duttons are far from done defending
their land from outsiders and competitors

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:05.200
and a handful of new faces are coming to Big
Sky Country for the new season.

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:10.720
These include Lost alum Josh Holloway and
The New World star Q'orianka Kilcher.

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:16.200
Season 3 of Yellowstone is currently in production,
and is set to premiere on June 17, 2020.

